# Who has to review a pull request here.
#
# `main` is protected: a change reaches it through a pull request, and the
# branch requires an approving review FROM a code owner before it can merge.
# This file is the list of those code owners, so it is what decides who can
# unblock a pull request.
#
# Read the consequence before changing it. GitHub does not let an author
# approve their own pull request, so a pull request opened by kumanaya can
# never be approved by kumanaya. With a single code owner, that means a pull
# request opened by kumanaya cannot be merged at all until somebody reviews it
# from a second account. That is the intended trade: nothing lands unread, and
# the person who can land it is not the person who wrote it.
#
# `required_approving_review_count` on its own cannot express that. It says how
# many reviews are needed, not who counts as a reader.
* @kumanaya
